**Analysis of Search Results for Audi A4 Cabriolet TDI (B7):**

*   **Generations:** The A4 Cabriolet was B6 (2002-2005) and B7 (2005-2009) (Source 3, 9, 13, 14, 27). The TDI engines were available in the B7 (2.0 TDI, 2.5 TDI, 2.7 TDI, 3.0 TDI) (Source 1, 2, 4, 5, 6, 9, 10, 13, 24). I will focus on the B7 TDI models.
*   **TDI Engine Options (B7):** 2.0 TDI (140 HP, 236 lb-ft), 2.5 TDI V6 (163 HP, 258 lb-ft), 2.7 TDI V6 (180 HP), 3.0 TDI V6 (233 HP, 331 lb-ft) (Source 1, 2, 4, 5, 6, 9, 10, 13). The 2.0 TDI is a common variant.
*   **Performance (2.0 TDI 140 HP):** 0-60 mph in 9.2-10.1 seconds (Source 2, 4, 8, 13, 31). Top speed 129-132 mph (Source 1, 2, 4, 13).
*   **Performance (3.0 TDI 233 HP Quattro):** 0-60 mph in 6.9-7.1 seconds (Source 10, 12, 40). Top speed 150 mph (Source 5, 10).
*   **Drive Type:** FWD and Quattro AWD were available with TDI engines (Source 5, 9, 10, 13, 24).
*   **Transmission:** Manual, Multitronic CVT (FWD), and Tiptronic Automatic (Quattro) were available (Source 9, 13, 24, 25). Multitronic CVT has reliability concerns (Source 32). Tiptronic is a conventional auto.
*   **Fuel Economy (2.0 TDI):** Combined 37-44.1 mpg UK (Source 1, 2, 4, 8, 13, 15, 24).
*   **Fuel Economy (3.0 TDI Quattro):** Combined 35.8 mpg UK (Source 10, 12).
*   **CO2 Emissions (2.0 TDI):** 173 g/km (Source 1).
*   **CO2 Emissions (3.0 TDI Quattro):** 209 g/km (Not explicitly in results, but estimated based on MPG).
*   **Dimensions:** Length ~4573mm, Width ~1777mm, Height ~1391mm, Wheelbase ~2650mm (Source 2, 3, 4, 6, 8, 9, 14, 20, 37).
*   **Cargo Space:** 246L (hood down) - 315L (hood up) (Source 3, 4, 6, 8, 9, 14, 16, 20, 39). This is small.
*   **Rear Space:** Limited rear legroom due to soft top storage (Source 9, 16, 24).
*   **Ground Clearance:** ~10.9 cm / ~4.3 inches (Source 20). This is low.
*   **Turn Radius:** ~11.1m / ~36.4 ft (Source 4, 6, 10, 11). This is average.
*   **Seats:** 4 (Source 3, 8, 9, 13, 39).
*   **Reliability/Repair Risk:** 2.0 TDI has known issues like oil pump problems and injector recalls (Source 23, 35). 3.0 TDI is generally considered more robust but can have starting rattles (Source 32). Overall, Audi reliability is often considered average to slightly below average, with potentially higher repair costs than non-premium brands (Source 19, 28).
*   **Maintenance Cost:** Audi maintenance is generally higher than average (Source 28).
*   **Insurance Group:** Audi A4 models range from 19-41 (UK groups) (Source 33). Cabriolets and higher trims/engines would be in higher groups. 2.0 TDI is Group 31, 3.0 TDI is Group 35. (Based on Parkers, Source 15, 36). This is above average.
*   **Price (Used):** Prices vary significantly based on year, condition, mileage, and engine/trim. UK prices range from ~£2,500 to ~£5,000+ (Source 21, 29, 30, 34, 38). This is well below the new car average.
*   **Total Cost of Ownership:** Likely average to slightly above average for an older premium car due to potential maintenance/repair costs balancing low purchase price.
